@ 46.10 - Late Proto-Finnic to Savonian Vowel Shift
# citation: PM_Vanhanen “Long close-mid vowels have become diphthongs:” “In some dialects, they have shifted further to /uɑ/, /yæ/ and /iæ/ or /iɑ/ depending on front-back vowel harmony: /tieto/ to /tiɑto/ but /tietæ/ to /tiætæ/.” “These shifts have occurred in some eastern dialects.”
	{ e:[+long], ø:[+long], o:[+long] } > { ie, yø, uo }
	{ ɑ:[+long], æ:[+long], ɑi, æi } > { uɑ, iæ, ɑe, æe }
	{ ei, oi, øi } > { e:[+long], oe, øe }
	{ ɑu, ou } > { ɑ:[+long], o:[+long] }
	{ æy, øy } > { æ:[+long], ø:[+long] }
	eu > eo
	{ li, ni, ri, si } > { lʲi, nʲi, rʲi, sʲi }